the series now reproduces the tree it describes, and one hunk was in the wrong function

vendor/patches/cocotron is an ORPHAN. scripts/checks/buck-pin-patches-check.nu has been saying so
for a long time and buck-test.nu prints it every run:

  patches/cocotron: 29 patches -> NOTHING
  vendor/patches/cocotron (29 patches) is an ORPHAN: no manifest entry names it and no pin basename
  matches it, so it has never been applied to anything

vendor/pins/cocotron is a BUNDLED pin, checked into git, and scripts/buck-src.nu COPIES it into
vendor/src/cocotron. vendor/src is not tracked. So every cocotron change lives in exactly one place,
an untracked directory, and a materialisation silently reverts all of it. The patches are the only
record, and until now they did not reproduce the tree.

MEASURED, applying the series to a fresh copy of the pin:

  23 of 29 applied.
  3 were ALREADY IN THE PIN (the aarch64 ones, 0001 to 0003), which is why they refuse.
  3 applied only in part (0018, 0028, 0029): context drift, one hunk each.
  FIVE FILES then still differed from vendor/src/cocotron.

AND ONE OF THEM DIFFERED IN A WAY THAT MATTERS. O2Image.m has two near identical functions, and the
byte order default guard from #212 applied CLEANLY TO THE WRONG ONE: patch matched the context in
the neighbouring function. Replaying the series would have put the wxWidgets bitmap fix where it
does nothing, and the build would have succeeded. That is the failure mode the check warns about:
an unpatched or wrongly patched tree builds and reports as a pass.

WHAT THIS PATCH IS: the exact remaining delta of those five files, which moves the O2Image guard to
the function it was written for and carries what the three partial patches left behind.

VERIFIED, and this is the point of the patch rather than a note beside it:

  a fresh copy of vendor/pins/cocotron, plus every patch in this directory in order with --forward,
  plus this one, is BYTE FOR BYTE vendor/src/cocotron.

STILL NOT WIRED. Nothing applies these during materialisation; that is a change to how a pin is
staged and it has the whole port in its blast radius, so it is a separate deliberate step. What
changed today is that the record is now exact and replayable BY HAND, which it was not.
